            <ArticleTitle>Myocardial technetium-99m-tetrofosmin single-photon emission computed tomography compared with 18F-fluorodeoxyglucose imaging to assess myocardial viability.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1223-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Technetium-99m-tetrofosmin single-photon emission computed tomography at rest is practical for routine assessment of viability in patients with ischemic cardiomyopathy. However, underestimation of viability may occur compared with 18F-fluorodeoxyglucose single-photon emission computed tomography, especially in the inferoposterior and septal regions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
